{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And the Ark of the Covenant of HaShem journeyed before them, etc.</b> And all that night the cloud rested upon the Ark, for they could not travel three consecutive days, night and day, since we say: one who vows not to sleep for three days is lashed and sleeps immediately. And in the morning it would journey from upon the Ark, and the Levites would prepare their departures before the camps set out — and this is 'journeyed before them,' according to its plain sense: the journeying of the Ark during those three days was until they came to the wilderness of Paran. But when they came to the wilderness, they sent the spies, as it is written: ״וישלח אותם משה ממדבר פארן״, and then they journeyed without the Ark, as it is written: ״ויעפילו לעלות״ etc., ״וארון ברית ה' ומשה לא משו מתוך המחנה״ — and this was the first journey they made after those three days. And what is written 'a three days' journey' means 'in the manner of a three-day journey,' like ״כי ששת ימים עשה ה'״, which means 'in six days.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:04.336409980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}